      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Researches have shown anti-vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) agent is effective in treating neovascular eye diseases. The purpose of this study is to evaluate the efficacy and safety of intravitreal ranibizumab (IVR) injection combined trabeculectomy in the treatment of neovascular glaucoma (NVG), and compared it with Ahmed valve surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Thirty-six NVG patients (37 eyes) from the First Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang medical college, between January 1, 2014 and January 31, 2015, were included in this prospective, interventional clinical study. Eighteen NVG eyes were given IVR injection one week before trabeculectomy. Ahmed valve implantation surgery was performed in nineteen eyes. Ocular pain, best corrected visual acuity (BCVA), intraocular pressure (IOP) and surgical complications were evaluated before and after the surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "IOP was significantly decreased following IVR injection combined trabeculectomy treatment (baseline 57.1\u2009±\u20098.9 mmHg; week 1, 15.2\u2009±\u20094.3 mmHg p\u2009=\u20090.000; month 1, 16.9\u2009±\u20092.1 mmHg p\u2009=\u20090.000; month 3, 20.3\u2009±\u20097.7 mmHg p\u2009=\u20090.000; month 6, 19.7\u2009±\u20097.3 mmHg p\u2009=\u20090.000). There was a significant, though modest, BCVA improvement in sighted eyes of IVR group (baseline 2.42\u2009±\u20090.68, W1 1.80\u2009±\u20090.91, P\u2009=\u20090.013; M1 1.77\u2009±\u20090.93, p\u2009=\u20090.011). IVR injection combined trabeculectomy had less postoperative complications and lower failure ratio than Ahmed surgery (IVR 5.6 %, Ahmed 31.6 %)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The study revealed that IVR injection combined trabeculectomy was an effective and safe treatment for NVG. Compared with Ahmed surgery, IVR injection combined trabeculectomy had less complications and higher success ratio. (Chinese Clinical Registry, TRN ChiCTR-OPN-16008147, 3/24/2016, retrospectively registered)."
        }
      ]},
